---
/*
 * Premium is described as intended rather than available on purpose. There is no
 * billing code in raider-mate-service, so any sentence written in the present tense
 * about taking payment would be false today.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/legal-layout.astro';
import { COMPANY_URL, ORG_URL } from '../lib/brand';

export const prerender = false;

const UPDATED = '2026-08-20';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using the hosted instance of Raider Mate. Self-hosting is covered by the AGPL instead."
  updated={UPDATED}
>
  <h2>Who you are agreeing with</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are between you and{' '}
    <strong><a href={COMPANY_URL} rel="noreferrer">Phage Solutions, s.r.o.</a></strong>, a limited
    liability company registered in Slovakia at Lermontovova 911/3, 811 05 Bratislava. Company ID
    (IČO) 53151178, VAT ID (IČ DPH) SK2121316010, Commercial Register (ORSR) insert number 147154/B.
    Reach us at <a href="mailto:dpo@phage.sk">dpo@phage.sk</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    They cover <strong>the hosted instance only</strong>. Raider Mate is free software under the
    AGPL, and if you run your own copy these terms do not apply to you at all. The{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what the hosted instance does with your data.
  </p>

  <h2>What Raider Mate does</h2>
  <p>
    A Discord bot posts your raid nights and takes signups. A service works out a composition from
    those signups and from character data synced from Raider.IO. This dashboard is where a raid lead
    reads that composition, overrides it, and looks at the roster behind it.
  </p>

  <h2>Using it</h2>
  <p>
    You need a Discord account, and you have to be old enough to hold one. To add the bot to a
    server you need permission to do that in that server. Adding it means the people in it will have
    their signups and characters handled as the Privacy Policy describes, so tell them.
  </p>
  <p>Do not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use Raider Mate to harass anyone, or to store abusive content in notes or event titles;</li>
    <li>try to reach another guild's data;</li>
    <li>attack the service, flood it with requests, or work around its rate limits;</li>
    <li>resell access to the hosted instance as if it were yours.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Running your own instance and charging for it is a different matter. The AGPL permits that, and
    these terms do not restrict it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your guild's data</h2>
  <p>
    The roster, the signups and the compositions are your guild's, not ours. You give us permission
    to store and process them only so far as running the service needs, and for nothing else. We do
    not use them to train anything, and we do not sell them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Raid leads can move anyone anywhere in a composition, and Raider Mate writes down what they
    asked for without checking it. What a composition says is your raid lead's decision, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>Premium</h2>
  <p>
    Some of what Raider Mate can show, including the analysis views, is intended to sit behind a
    paid tier priced at <strong>€2.99 per month</strong> or <strong>€29.99 per year</strong>. Both
    prices include VAT, so what is written is what you pay. Payment will be handled by Stripe.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Premium is not open yet.</strong> There is no billing in the service today, nothing can be
    charged, and no payment details exist. When it does open, these terms will gain the parts that a paid
    subscription needs, including how to cancel and how refunds work, and you will not be charged under
    terms you have not seen.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We run the hosted instance carefully but we do not promise it will be up when you need it. There
    is no uptime guarantee. Raid nights have gone ahead without software for twenty years and can do
    so again.
  </p>
  <p>
    Raider Mate depends on Discord and on Raider.IO. When either is down or changes how it works,
    parts of Raider Mate stop working, and that is outside our control.
  </p>

  <h2>Stopping</h2>
  <p>
    Remove the bot from your server whenever you like. That server's data is deleted within 30 days,
    as the Privacy Policy sets out.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may suspend or remove access to the hosted instance if it is being used against the rules
    above, or if we have to for legal or security reasons. Where it is reasonable to warn you first,
    we will.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we ever shut the hosted instance down we will give notice in time for guilds to export what
    matters or move to their own instance.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not promise</h2>
  <p>
    Raider Mate is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we exclude implied warranties,
    and we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, for lost raid progress, or for
    anything arising from a composition a raid lead chose.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing here limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or
    for anything else that cannot be limited by law. If you are a consumer, your statutory rights
    are unaffected by anything on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When these terms change, the date at the top changes. A change that materially affects you will
    be announced somewhere you will see it rather than slipped in here.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    Slovak law governs these terms, and the Slovak courts have jurisdiction. If you are a consumer
    resident elsewhere in the EU, this does not deprive you of the protection of the mandatory rules
    of your own country, and you may bring proceedings there.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:dpo@phage.sk">dpo@phage.sk</a>. The{' '}
    <a href={ORG_URL} rel="noreferrer">source</a> is public if you would rather read what it does than
    what we say it does.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
